Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough (@fd-mcdonough: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18
James M. McDonough. Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics: Physics, Mathematics and Applications, University of Kentucky, 2009. [University repository and complete text](https://uknowledge.uky.edu/me_textbooks/1/).

Read the complete book progressively, including mathematical development and substantial independent problems. Use it as an introductory engineering spine while the Records explain how a physical observation becomes a model and a calculation. Compare the physical assumptions with [Introdução à Mecânica dos Fluidos e aos Fenômenos de Transporte — Gobbi and colleagues](Mecanica-dos-Fluidos-e-Transportes-Gobbi-Dias.lingua#r_1F9KHVCP86X68RR7DTZASE5F1J), then deepen analytical methods in [Intermediate Fluid Mechanics — James Liburdy](Intermediate-Fluid-Mechanics-Liburdy.lingua#r_45KKWKB7DTN9MMQ951P62JHH5N) and [Fluid Mechanics — David Tong](Fluid-Mechanics-Tong.lingua#r_3SP698XHQFSZZ6N9Q22NESHMEA).

The university identifies the 2009 work and hosts its full text as an archived teaching resource. Automated PDF retrieval returned 403 during source inspection; the catalogue was accessible. No page-level inspection or blanket adaptation licence is asserted. Free authorized reading and the copyright notices of a selected copy are distinct. The source file remains external.

